The biggest problem with named weapons is that some of them are simply
not useful compared with the others.  In particular, the
monster-specific weapons don't help much.  A monster-specific weapon
is no better than a general-purpose artifact, and often worse!

To make this more interesting, have the monster-specific weapon be
absolutely devastating against that specific class.  Instead of merely
doing double damage, triple the damage or add larger die rolls.  Also,
have it terrify the opponent, who will recognize it.  This would be
easy to do by simply using the Magicbane code.

Other things to do would be to add turning effects to Sunsword, or to
make Demonbane silver.

Let's face it.  Who actually uses Dragonbane against dragons?
Trollsbane against trolls?  Demonbane against demons?  The general
purpose artifacts are the ones you've added the enchantments to.  They
are simply more effective.

When I get Ogresmasher, I generally ditch it as extra weight.  I'm
often annoyed at finding a monster-specific artifact, because it means
that useful artifacts are harder to get!

Since they are, after all, special high-quality weapons, even
monster-specific artifacts should have some bonus against non-specific
opponents.  Say, an extra +1 or +2.  Between that and real
effectiveness against some common kind of monster, one of these
artifacts would be a real find, instead of extra baggage.

Finally, come up with some better names:  Demonbane, Trollsbane,
Werebane, Dragonbane, Magicbane...enough!  I'm sure there are examples
in literature of weapons used against various monsters, or we can just
come up with names, and use our own mythology!

Let's see:  Moonsword against lycanthropes.  Dragonslayer is obvious.
Piercer for Magicbane...and so on.  Make sure the special messages are
there upon a hit, so players know what is happening.  In fact, make
all effective hits with special purpose artifacts give a message.

Come up with some truly unholy weapon that works well on angels.  That
will give a recommended method for dealing with Archons.

Make some artifact missile weapon, such as a bow.  Make it less
effective than hand-to-hand, of course, but still worthwhile.
That spinning thing from Krull would work (although it would have to
be scaled back a bit).

